This repository holds three different kinds of work, and one licence cannot
sensibly cover all of them. MIT alone was the wrong fit, because most of what
is here is writing rather than software.


1. THE WRITING - Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

Covers all prose, headings, page copy, guidance, and the diagrams drawn as
inline SVG.

Full legal text: see LICENSE-CONTENT in this repository.
Plain summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You are free to share and adapt this material, for any purpose including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit to Zolsi.CC, link to the
licence, and indicate whether you made changes.

Why this licence. This is safety information, and it is only useful if it
travels. A school, a charity, a youth worker or a translator should be able to
take it, adapt it, and pass it on without asking anyone. The attribution
requirement costs a reuser almost nothing, and the requirement to state that
changes were made matters here: altered safety advice should not be able to
present itself as ours.


